1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:08.171
This video demonstrates how to perform a front-of-the-eye examination using the anterior segment loop of the Arclight device.

2
00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:11.267
Start with hand hygiene and introduce yourself.

3
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:17.901
Confirm the identity of the patient, explain the examination and gain consent to perform it.

4
00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:23.650
Initially take a few seconds to observe both eyes at the same time.

5
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.515
Look at the periorbitor, eyelids and eyes, commenting on any swelling,

6
00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:33.380
redness and discharge, as well as prominence of the eyes or

7
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.940
abnormal eyelid position.

8
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.100
Then perform a magnified examination using the arclight.

9
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.433
Switch on the white light and hold the device close to your eye.

10
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:44.100
Slowly approach

11
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.750
the patient's right eye first until it is in focus.

12
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.340
This will be at around 6

13
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:48.604
centimeters.

14
00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:52.300
Ask the patient to move their eye outwards and inwards, then up and down,

15
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.278
while gently holding their eyelids.

16
00:00:54.278 --> 00:00:55.860
Systematically noting the different

17
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.552
structures seen, thinking of them in groups.

18
00:00:58.552 --> 00:01:00.860
The first group includes the upper

19
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.171
and lower eyelashes and lid margins.

20
00:01:04.171 --> 00:01:09.690
The second includes a conjunctiva and sclera and the lower

21
00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.135
forenicks.

22
00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:12.805
The third group is the cornea.

23
00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:16.810
The junction of this was a sclera called olimbus

24
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.237
and the pupil, surrounded by the iris.

25
00:01:19.237 --> 00:01:22.010
Once you have finished noting all these structures,

26
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.810
move on to assessing the anterior chamber depth.

27
00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.610
The anterior chamber is the space between the

28
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.795
cornea and the iris.

29
00:01:28.795 --> 00:01:32.350
By shining the light from the temporal side, the depths of the

30
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.171
anterior chamber can be assessed.

31
00:01:34.171 --> 00:01:37.450
A shadow on the nasal iris can suggest a

32
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.061
shallow anterior chamber.

33
00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:43.356
This is a normal examination with no shadow.

34
00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:44.430
Now select

35
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.465
the blue light on the arc light.

36
00:01:46.465 --> 00:01:48.790
With fluorescing dye, the tear film, areas of

37
00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.463
epithelial loss and disease will be highlighted.

38
00:01:51.463 --> 00:01:52.990
The dye fluoresces brightly

39
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.217
with the blue light.

40
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:57.590
Recording a diagram, the sight and size of areas of epithelial

41
00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.201
the loss and disease.

42
00:01:59.201 --> 00:02:02.021
Finish by examining the superior tarsal plate.

43
00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.230
Place a cotton

44
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:08.230
bud on the upper lid, then gently lift the lashes upwards while slowly pressing downwards

45
00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.120
with the bud.

46
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.570
Initially observe with a naked eye, then bring in the arc light for a magnified

47
00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.070
view.

48
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.570
Repeat this examination on the other eye.

49
00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.070
Afterwards thank the patient, summarizing

50
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.290
the records of findings and repeat hand hygiene.

51
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.510
Please have a look at our other University

52
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.510
the Andrews Arc Light Project Videos.
